py tools/bench/c60c_astcheck.py diag_c60_n4_localbinding.py     # the cycle-60 target it was written for
```

- **Claim predicts:** the first FAILs only on 7 (vetoing `diag_s58_boolwire.py`, whose three artefacts this project has *accepted* — `STATUS.md:9`), and the second is 12/12. Read together: one dead check, the rest sound.
- **My alternative predicts:** the first FAILs on 7 *and* its detail lines show 2/8/9 passing vacuously against a brief that never proposed those routes — the file discriminates nothing about cycle 62 in either direction. Combined with the already-recorded `c62e_astcheck.log` 12/12 on the dispatch that produced no artefact, that settles it: write the cycle-62 gate.

The first command alone is near-certain in outcome (I can read `move_in` at `diag_s58_boolwire.py:162,:889`), so it is confirmation, not discrimination — the discriminating content is in the **detail columns of checks 2/8/9**, not in the pass/fail. Read those, not the summary line.

